sn1.32:14.4 starts: Are not worth even a fraction
sn1.34:6.1 starts: “He abandoned reckoning, did not assume conceit;
sn1.34:6.2 starts: He cut off craving here for name-and-form.
sn1.34:6.3 starts: Though devas and humans search for him
sn1.34:6.4 starts: Here and beyond, in the heavens and all
sn1.34:6.5 starts: They do not find the one whose knots
sn1.34:6.6 starts: The one untroubled, free of longing.”
sn1.34:7.4 starts: “Are they to be praised who venerate him,
sn1.34:7.5 starts: The best of men, faring for the good
